### 35. Section. Claim Amount

(1)	The claim amount is:

1)	in claims for recovery of money — the sum to be recovered;  

2)	in claims for recovery of property — the value of the property to be recovered;  

3)	in claims for recovery of maintenance — the total sum of payments for one year;  

4)	in claims for fixed-term payments and benefits — the total sum of all payments or benefits, but not more than for three years;  

5)	in claims for indefinite or lifetime payments and benefits — the total sum of all payments and benefits for three years;  

6)	in claims for reduction or increase of payments or benefits — the sum by which the payments or benefits are reduced or increased, but not more than for one year;  

7)	in claims for termination of payments or benefits — the total sum of remaining payments or benefits, but not more than for one year;  

8)	in claims for early termination of a lease or rental agreement — the total sum of payments for the remaining term of the agreement, but not more than for three years;  

9)	in claims for property rights to immovable property — its value, but not less than its cadastral value;  

10)	in claims consisting of several independent pecuniary claims — the total sum of all claims;  

11)	in claims for termination of a transaction or declaring it invalid — the sum of the contested transaction.  

(2)	The claim amount is indicated by the claimant. If the indicated claim amount manifestly does not correspond to the actual value of the property to be recovered, the claim amount is determined by the court.  
(With amendments made by the law of 02.09.2004, which enters into force on 07.10.2004.)

### 36. Section. Additional State Fee Payment

(1)	For a claim that is difficult to evaluate at the time of submission, the judge determines the amount of the state fee in advance. The final

amount of the state fee is determined by the court when examining the case.  

(2)	If the claim amount is increased, except for the addition of interest and increments, the state fee shall be paid additionally accordingly.  

36.	1 Section. Crediting of State Fee

The fee paid for an application for a European order for payment in accordance with Regulation No. 1896/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council shall be credited to the state fee for the claim if the defendant has notified an objection to the European order for payment and claim proceedings are continued.  
(In the wording of the law of 08.09.2011, which enters into force on 30.09.2011.)

### 37. Section. Refund of State Fee

(1)	The state fee paid shall be refunded in full or in part in the following cases:

1)	if a larger fee has been paid than required by law;  

2)	if the court refuses to accept the application;  

3)	if proceedings in the case are terminated on the grounds that the examination of the case is not subject to the court;  

4)	if the claim is left without examination on the grounds that the interested person who applied to the court has not complied with the out-of-court examination procedure established for the relevant category of cases, or the application has been submitted by a person lacking civil procedural capacity;  

5)	if the court has approved a settlement — in the amount of 50 percent of the state fee paid for proceedings in the court of the relevant instance;  

6)	if the court refuses to initiate appellate proceedings in accordance with the seventh part of Section 440.8 of this law — in the amount of 50 percent of the state fee paid;  

7)	if the grounds for termination of proceedings are the claimant's waiver of the claim because a mediation agreement has been reached, which is certified by a written confirmation of the mediation result issued by a mediator — in the amount of 50 percent of the state fee paid.  

(2)	(Declared invalid by the judgment of the Constitutional Court of 02.11.2020)

(3)	The court or judge, on its own initiative or upon a person's application, adopts a decision on the refund of the state fee if it establishes any of the cases mentioned in the first part of this section. An application for refund of the state fee may be submitted to the court where the case is located within one year from the day when the grounds for refund of the state fee arose.  
(With amendments made by the laws of 31.10.2002., 19.06.2003., 20.12.2010., 08.09.2011., 29.11.2012., 20.03.2014.,
22.05.2014., 29.10.2015., the judgment of the Constitutional Court of 02.11.2020 and the law of 11.11.2021, which enters into force on
01.12.2021.)

### 38. Section. Registry Fee

(Deleted by the law of 11.11.2021, which enters into force on 01.12.2021.)

### 39. Section. Expenses Related to Case Examination

(1)	Expenses related to case examination are:

1)	sums to be paid to witnesses and experts;  

2)	expenses related to the interrogation of witnesses or the performance of inspections on site;  

3)	expenses related to the search for the defendant or a witness;  

4)	expenses related to the execution of a court judgment;  

5)	expenses related to the preparation, delivery, issuance, translation of court summonses and other court documents and the return of written evidence;  

6)	expenses related to the preparation and issuance of an announcement text;  

7)	expenses related to securing a claim or interim protection;  

8)	(deleted from 01.01.2012. by the law of 31.10.2002.).  

(2)	The sums to be paid to witnesses and experts, as well as the amount and calculation procedure for expenses related to the interrogation of witnesses or the performance of inspections on site, the search for the defendant or a witness, the preparation, delivery, issuance, translation of court summonses and other court documents, the return of written evidence, the preparation and issuance of an announcement text and securing a claim or interim protection shall be determined by the Cabinet of Ministers.  
(With amendments made by the laws of 31.10.2002., 25.03.2021. and 11.11.2021., which enters into force on 01.12.2021.)

### 40. Section. Procedure for Payment of Expenses Related to Case Examination

(1)	The sums of expenses to be paid to witnesses and experts, or the sums necessary for payment of expenses for the interrogation of witnesses or the performance of inspections on site, the translation of court summonses and other court documents, the preparation and issuance of an announcement text and securing a claim or interim protection, shall be paid by the party that has made the relevant request. The sums necessary for payment of expenses for the preparation, delivery, issuance of copies of court summonses and other court documents and the return of written evidence shall be paid by the state.  

(2)	If, at the request of Latvia, evidence is obtained or court documents are issued to a person abroad, the sums of expenses that the competent authority of a foreign state requests to be paid before or reimbursed after the execution of the request shall be paid by the party that has made the relevant request.  

(3)	If both parties have submitted the request referred to in the first or second part of this section, they shall pay the requested sums in equal amounts.  

(4)	If the request referred to in the first or second part of this section has been submitted by the court or judge on its own initiative in the cases provided for in this law, the necessary sum shall be paid by the state.  

(5)	The sums referred to in this section shall not be paid by a party that is exempt from payment of court expenses.  
(In the wording of the law of 05.02.2009. with amendments made by the laws of 25.03.2021. and 11.11.2021., which enters into force on 01.12.2021.)

