### 43. Section. Exceptions to General Rules on Court Costs

(1)	Exempted from payment of court costs to state revenues:

1)	plaintiffs — in claims for recovery of wages and other employee claims arising from employment legal relations or related thereto;  

11)	plaintiffs — in claims arising from an agreement on performance of work, if the plaintiff is a person serving a sentence in a place of imprisonment;  

12)	applicants — for an application for insolvency proceedings of a legal person or natural person, if the enforcement of a court decision on recovery of wages has been recognised as impossible in the procedure established by this law;  

2)	plaintiffs — in claims arising from personal injuries resulting in mutilation or other health damage or death of a person;  

3)	plaintiffs — in claims for recovery of maintenance for a child or parent, as well as in claims for establishment of paternity if the claim is brought simultaneously with a claim for recovery of maintenance for a child;  

31) applicants — for recognition or recognition and enforcement of a foreign decision on recovery of maintenance for a child or parent;  

4)	plaintiffs — in claims for compensation for damage and non-pecuniary harm resulting from a criminal offence or administrative offence;  

5)	prosecutors, those state or municipal institutions which have been granted by law the right to defend in court the rights and legally protected interests of other persons;  

6)	applicants — for restriction of legal capacity of a person due to mental or other health disorders, review of restriction of legal capacity or restoration of legal capacity;  

61) applicants — for establishment and termination of temporary guardianship;  

7)	applicants — for restriction of legal capacity of a person and establishment of guardianship due to wasteful or extravagant lifestyle, as well as due to excessive use of alcohol or other intoxicating substances;  

8)	defendants — in cases concerning reduction of court-awarded maintenance for a child or parent and reduction of payments awarded by a court in claims arising from personal injuries resulting in mutilation or other health damage or death of a person;  

9)	(deleted as of 01.01.2012. by the law of 31.10.2002.);  

91) applicants — in cases concerning unlawful removal of a child across a border or retention;  

10)	administrators — in claims brought on behalf of persons for whom insolvency proceedings of a legal person and insolvency proceedings of a natural person have been declared, if these persons are participants in or victims of the respective legal transaction or unlawful act in connection with which the claim is brought;  

11)	creditors — in enforcement cases concerning recoveries to state revenues;  

111) creditors — in enforcement cases where recovery is to be made in accordance with a uniform instrument permitting enforcement in the requested Member State;  

12)	tax (duty) administration — in applications in insolvency proceedings cases of legal persons;  

13)	Office of Citizenship and Migration Affairs — in cases concerning deprivation of Latvian citizenship;  

14)	State Social Insurance Agency — in cases concerning recovery of financial resources to the state budget in respect of overpayment of social insurance services or state social benefits and payment of social insurance services or state social benefits in connection with road traffic accidents;  

15)	applicants — for temporary protection against violence;  

16)	a party receiving state-provided legal aid in a case;  

161) a party recognised as a whistleblower or being his or her relative or related person within the meaning of the Whistleblowing Law;  

17)	applicants — for confirmation of adoption;  

18)	sworn notary — in cases concerning cancellation of discharge of a natural person from debt obligations, if the sworn notary has prepared a notarial act on discharge of a natural person from debt obligations;  

19)	complainants — concerning refusal of a sworn notary to certify an application for discharge of a natural person from debt obligations, as well as concerning refusal to discharge a natural person from debt obligations;  

20)	plaintiffs — in consumer collective actions.  

(2)	If a prosecutor, those state or municipal institutions which have been granted by law the right to defend in court the rights and legally protected interests of other persons, withdraws from an application submitted on behalf of another person, but that person requests examination of the case on the merits, court costs shall be paid in accordance with general rules.  

(3)	Parties shall also be exempted from payment of court costs to state revenues in other cases provided for by law.  

(4)	The court or judge, taking into account the financial situation of a natural person, fully or partially exempts it from payment of court costs to state revenues, as well as postpones payment of court costs awarded to state revenues or divides it into instalments.  

(5)	In claims for dissolution of marriage, at the request of the plaintiff, the judge postpones payment of the state fee or divides it into instalments if the plaintiff has care of a minor child.  
(With amendments made by the laws of 20.06.2001., 31.10.2002., 19.06.2003., 07.09.2006., 01.11.2007., 05.02.2009.,
30.09.2010., 09.06.2011., 08.09.2011., 15.03.2012., 29.11.2012., 13.02.2014., 29.10.2015., 10.12.2015., 08.12.2016.,
01.06.2017.,  22.06.2017.,  14.12.2017.,  31.05.2018.,  28.02.2019.,  11.11.2021.,  15.06.2021.,  16.03.2023.  and
14.09.2023., which enters into force on 15.10.2023. Paragraph four, insofar as it does not provide a private law legal person with the right to request that the court decide on its exemption from the obligation to pay the state fee for submission of a statement of claim, has been declared invalid as of 01.10.2023. by the judgment of the Constitutional Court of 17.02.2023., which enters into force on 20.02.2023.)

43.1 Section. Security Deposit

(1)	Security deposit shall be paid in the following amount:

1)	for an interlocutory appeal, except for an interlocutory appeal against a decision refusing exemption from security deposit or payment of court costs to state revenues, — 70 euros;  

2)	for a cassation appeal — 300 euros;  

3)	for a complaint concerning actions of an insolvency proceedings administrator (hereinafter — administrator) or sworn bailiff, or sworn notary — 70 euros;  

4)	for an application for reopening of a case due to newly discovered circumstances — 300 euros.  

(2)	Security deposit need not be paid by persons who are exempted from state fee in accordance with law. The court or judge, taking into account the financial situation of a natural person, may fully or partially exempt a person from payment of security deposit.  
(In the wording of the law of 25.03.2021., which enters into force on 20.04.2021. The second sentence of paragraph two, insofar as these provisions do not provide a private law legal person with the right to request that the court decide on its exemption from the obligation to pay security deposit for submission of an interlocutory appeal, has been declared invalid by the judgment of the Constitutional Court of 23.02.2022., which enters into force on 25.02.2022.)

43.2 Section. Refund of Security Deposit

(1)	If the court fully or in part revokes or amends the appealed or contested court decision or fully or partially grants a complaint concerning actions of an insolvency proceedings administrator, sworn bailiff or sworn notary, the security deposit shall be refunded. If the appeal or application is rejected, the security deposit shall not be refunded.  

(2)	Security deposit shall also be refunded or not refunded in other cases established by this law.  

(3)	Security deposit shall be refunded from state budget funds on the basis of a decision of the court or judge.  
(In the wording of the law of 25.03.2021., which enters into force on 20.04.2021.)

43.	3 Section. Payment of Court Costs and Security Deposit to Incorrect State Budget Account

If court costs or security deposit have been paid to an incorrect account of the Court Administration, State Revenue Service or Supreme Court in the State Treasury, then these court costs and security deposit shall be transferred by the Court Administration, State Revenue Service or Supreme Court to the appropriate account on the basis of a decision in the form of a resolution by the judge who has established it.  
(In the wording of the law of 25.03.2021., which enters into force on 20.04.2021.)

